[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/QaWstlC.png[/img][/center]

ESP Explorer AE is an in-game explorer and utility menu for Fallout 4 on Steam.

Browse your loaded plugins, find items, manage your inventory, or spawn an NPC without leaving the game. Search and filters help you find what you need, while favorites keep useful records close at hand.

[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/QaWstlC.png[/img][/center]

[center][b][img]https://i.imgur.com/KRjnKOf.png[/img][/b][/center]

[list]
[*]Browse ESP, ESM, and ESL plugins, with dedicated browsers for items, NPCs, cells, objects, spells, and perks.[/*]
[*]Add items, spawn NPCs, teleport to cells, and add or remove spells and perks.[/*]
[*]Manage your inventory and inspect equipment, item stacks, and attached weapon or armor mods.[/*]
[*]Search across plugins and records, with advanced filters for larger mod lists.[/*]
[*]Save favorites, revisit recent records, and copy names or IDs from the menu.[/*]
[*]View record details, plugin diagnostics, action history, and searchable logs.[/*]
[*]Use Explore, Inventory, Player & World, and Tools, with adjustable source, results, and inspector panes.[/*]
[*]Follow record links, pin inspectors, compare base records or inventory instances, and return to the original search and layout.[/*]
[*]Save views and collections with notes. Search selected plugins or collections with structured fields and Unicode-aware ordinary search.[/*]
[*]Assemble base items across searches in the basket, save reusable kits, review the aggregate items and ammunition, and inspect grouped results in Action History.[/*]
[*]Open Commands & Shortcuts with Ctrl+K, including exact FormID lookup and saved views.[/*]
[*]Customize the interface with themes, font sizes, languages, and optional Pip-Boy color sync.[/*]
[*]Keyboard, mouse, and optional gamepad navigation.[/*]
[/list]

Settings also let you rebind the menu key, choose a startup tab, and adjust how the menu behaves while you play.

[center][size=2]Some shipped translations were created with LLM assistance and may contain mistakes. English is the reference language.[/size][/center]

[center][size=2]Custom themes and translations can be added through the files in Data/Interface/ESPExplorerAE.[/size][/center]


[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/QaWstlC.png[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/4xgIdrp.png[/img][/center]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://f4se.silverlock.org/]F4SE[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/47327]Address Library for F4SE Plugins[/url] for your exact Fallout4.exe version.[/*]
[*]Install the mod with your mod manager, or merge the archive's Data folder into your Fallout 4 game folder.[/*]
[*]Launch the game through F4SE.[/*]
[/list]

Load a save or start a game, then press INSERT to open the menu. You can change the key in Settings.

Your preferences and favorites are saved in Data/F4SE/Plugins/ESPExplorerAE.ini. Saved views, collections, kits, and layouts use ESPExplorerAE.workspace.ini in the same folder. Keep both files when updating. The workspace manager supports clipboard import/export with a preview of missing records; importing or loading a kit never executes it.

Selection and double-click inspect by default. Gameplay actions have explicit controls; Settings offers an opt-in for the previous double-click actions. The basket gives base items; Duplicate Item copies a chosen live inventory instance. Review Kit shows aggregated quantities and ammunition before giving anything, and Action History reports each result without automatic retries.

[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/QaWstlC.png[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/vCq3zR1.png[/img][/center]

[list]
[*]Steam Fallout 4 1.11.240 with F4SE 0.7.9.[/*]
[*]Steam Fallout 4 1.11.221 with F4SE 0.7.8.[/*]
[*]Steam Fallout 4 1.11.191 with F4SE 0.7.7.[/*]
[/list]

Each version requires its matching Address Library file. Other game versions, GOG, and VR are not supported.

[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/QaWstlC.png[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/BbRvQ3C.png[/img][/center]

If you run into a problem, please include:

[list]
[*]What happened.[/*]
[*]How to reproduce it.[/*]
[*]ESP Explorer AE, Fallout4.exe, and F4SE versions, plus the Address Library file you installed.[/*]
[*]Any relevant mods or settings.[/*]
[*]A screenshot and ESPExplorerAE.log from Documents/My Games/Fallout4/F4SE if available.[/*]
[/list]

Report bugs here:
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/DeisDev/ESP-Explorer-AE/issues]Github[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/102223?tab=bugs]Nexus Bug Tracker[/url][/*]
[/list]

